{
  "source": "video-audit/transformer-repair-2026-09-10/edited.wav",
  "duration": 185.7,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.74,
      "text": "When you type a prompt into ChatGPT, you are sending it a sequence of words."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.24,
      "end": 10.1,
      "text": "Underneath the interface, the AI splits your text into small pieces, called tokens."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.9,
      "end": 16.8,
      "text": "Each token is assigned an embedding, which is a specific row of numbers that represents its baseline starting meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.5,
      "end": 20.04,
      "text": "That starting row of numbers is only a foundation."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.74,
      "end": 27.92,
      "text": "To determine what a word actually means in your specific sentence, the AI has to evaluate the surrounding words, the context."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.92,
      "end": 32.9,
      "text": "This graphic illustrates two primary problems context solves."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.9,
      "end": 34.8,
      "text": "First, different meanings."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.6,
      "end": 39.08,
      "text": "Light means brightness for a lamp, but not heavy for a suitcase."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.24,
      "end": 40.8,
      "text": "Second, pronouns."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.5,
      "end": 45.34,
      "text": "If the cat drank the milk because it was thirsty, it is the cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.9,
      "end": 47.74,
      "text": "If it was fresh, it's the milk."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.04,
      "end": 56.22,
      "text": "Earlier AI models process text strictly in sequence, reading one single word at a time, moving linearly from left to right."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.22,
      "end": 58.7,
      "text": "Look at how earlier AI read sentences."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.4,
      "end": 66.86,
      "text": "Because it processed words in strict order, information from cat had to be carried forward step by step down a long, fragile path to define it."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.34,
      "end": 69.32,
      "text": "In longer passages, the AI struggled."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.64,
      "end": 75.76,
      "text": "In 2017, a team of researchers at Google published a paper titled Attention is All You Need."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.22,
      "end": 80.66,
      "text": "They introduced a new architecture called the transformer, which is the T in ChatGPT."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.26,
      "end": 84.78,
      "text": "This demonstrates how a transformer processes the exact same sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.78,
      "end": 88.62,
      "text": "Instead of a linear sequence, the complete message arrives together."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.24,
      "end": 96.96,
      "text": "However, the AI still needs a mathematical way to determine which of these words actually matter to each other."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.48,
      "end": 100.74,
      "text": "Identifying those specific relationships is only the first step."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.38,
      "end": 108.28,
      "text": "The AI must then use those connections to mathematically update the row of numbers, the embedding, that represents the token."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.5,
      "end": 112.72,
      "text": "This happens in two main steps, starting with attention."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.72,
      "end": 122.82,
      "text": "The attention mechanism calculates relevance and blends surrounding context directly into the target token's numbers, feeding data from cat back to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.36,
      "end": 127.52,
      "text": "Then, transformation applies fixed patterns to process those blended numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.9,
      "end": 130.18,
      "text": "Let's apply this mechanism."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.84,
      "end": 134.52,
      "text": "In the first panel, turn on and carry provide context."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.0,
      "end": 139.92,
      "text": "It refers to the cat if the cat is thirsty, but it refers to the milk if the milk is fresh."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.78,
      "end": 152.2,
      "text": "By mapping how words interact across an entire message, the model can resolve these simple ambiguities and eventually handle the more complex logic found in sarcasm and idioms."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.6,
      "end": 156.76,
      "text": "This graphic demonstrates why word order is critical."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.74,
      "end": 163.5,
      "text": "Dog bites man, and man bites dog use identical tokens for entirely different events."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.22,
      "end": 168.38,
      "text": "Without position data, the transformer interprets a scattered cloud of words."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.38,
      "end": 170.72,
      "text": "Positional encoding solves this."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.3,
      "end": 176.72,
      "text": "By assigning numerical tags to track each word's specific place, it restores sequential structure."
    },
    {
      "start": 178.1,
      "end": 179.28,
      "text": "Attention is all you need."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.9,
      "end": 183.16,
      "text": "AI uses relationships between words to help interpret your message."
    }
  ],
